{
	"Site": "Nexus",
	"Id": 54968,
	"Name": "Stardew Modded and Vanilla NPC Schedule Fixes",
	"Author": "aerinanxiety",
	"Description": "[b][color=#d4d4d8][size=5]What it does[/size][/color][/b]\n<br />[list]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Stops NPCs from different mods from standing on top of each other in their daily schedules[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Fixes overlapping NPCs at modded festivals like Ridgeside's Gathering or Zuzu Block Party, also fixes vanilla overlaps at festivals.[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Covers the smaller festivals that run on normal schedules: the Desert Festival, Night Market, Trout Derby and SquidFest, plus festival days added by SVE, East Scarp, Sunberry Village and Law and Order[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Moves NPCs out of the water when a map mod reshapes a beach or pond under a spot written for the vanilla map[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Gives NPCs who were sharing a single chair, stool, bench or shop till a spot of their own[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Keeps shopkeepers behind their counters, and never parks an NPC where you stand to buy something[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Keeps NPCs off festival decorations, stalls and the spots where you’re warped in for the main event[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[/list][left][color=#D4D4D8][b][size=5]How it works[/size][/b][/color][/left]\n<br />[list]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Only moves NPCs a tile or two, and only for the one step of their day that collides. The rest of their schedule, their animations and their dialogue stay untouched[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Every new spot is open floor the NPC can actually walk to, free at that time, and clear of furniture and props[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Checked against every version of each map: optional map patches, story stages, seasonal edits and the Community Center’s ruined, restored and Joja states[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]Each fix only turns on when all the mods involved are installed. It does nothing for mods you don’t have[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[/list][left][color=#D4D4D8][b][size=5]NPCs Edited (You don't need all of them, just whatever you want to patch!)[/size][/b][/color][/left]\n<br />[spoiler][list]\n<br />[*][b]Stardew Valley Expanded:[/b] Alesia, Brianna, Brock, Cassandra, Charlie, Claire, Cordelia, Freya, Marlon, Martin, Morgan, Morris, Sophia, Susan, Victor[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Ridgeside Village:[/b] Aguar, Alissa, Anton, Bert, Carmen, Corine, Ezekiel, Flor, Freddie, Irene, Jeric, June, Kenneth, Kimpoi, Lenny, Lola, Lorenzo, Louie, Maddie, Maive, Olga, Paula, Philip, Pika, Shanice, Sonny, Ysabelle, Yuuma[/*]\n<br />[*][b]East Scarp:[/b] Aideen, Corwin, Dale, Edith, Eloise, Jacob, Jade, Jasper, Jessie, Josephine, Juliet, Kataryna, Michael, Rosa, Tori, Tristan[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Sunberry Village:[/b] Derya, Elias, Ezra, Maia, Moon, Silas, plus Dao, Jonghyuk and Spanner, and Rose (Rose and the Alchemist)[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Adventurer’s Guild Expanded:[/b] Gabriel, Silly, Zinnia[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Boarding House:[/b] Gregory, Joel, Sheila[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Cape Stardew:[/b] Morrigan[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Coal Point Farm:[/b] Ashida, Isaac, Marcus, Mora[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Defense Division:[/b] Edward, Isis, Lee, Miranda[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Desert Expansion:[/b] Laila[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Downhill Project:[/b] Anderson, Julia[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Hidden Place:[/b] Lowell[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Law and Order:[/b] Russell, Shannon[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Lunna - Astray in Stardew Valley:[/b] Bianka, Lunna, Raphael[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Rupnan Collection Remake:[/b] Aurelian, Junimi, Kaelen, Victoria, Xalathar[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Stardew Kids Expansion:[/b] Adrian, Douglas, James, Tina, Vanessa[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Sword &amp; Sorcery:[/b] Cirrus, Dandelion, Hector, Mateo, Roslin[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Trolley Expansion:[/b] Kaho, Koda, Ranger Taro[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Visit Mount Vapius:[/b] Celestine, Gavin[/*]\n<br />[/list][b]Standalone NPC mods[/b]\n<br />[list]\n<br />[*][b]Dead Boy Detectives:[/b] Charles, Edwin, Crystal, Jenny, Monty, Niko, the Cat King[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Bear Family:[/b] Gudrun, Gunnar, Sigurd, Teren[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Alecto the Witch:[/b] Alecto and Kevin the crow[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Boothill:[/b] Boothill, Clementine[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Eli &amp; Dylan:[/b] Eli, Dylan[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Jorts and Jean:[/b] Jean, Jorts[/*]\n<br />[*][b]Always Raining in the Valley:[/b] Henry, Sterling[/*]\n<br />[*][b]One NPC each:[/b]\n<br />[list]\n<br />[*]Aliyah[/*]\n<br />[*]Annetta[/*]\n<br />[*]Aspen[/*]\n<br />[*]Audrey[/*]\n<br />[*]Aurel[/*]\n<br />[*]Aymeric[/*]\n<br />[*]Cambria (Metalcore Goes Cottagecore)[/*]\n<br />[*]Clark[/*]\n<br />[*]Darcy[/*]\n<br />[*]Daulton[/*]\n<br />[*]Elian[/*]\n<br />[*]Enya[/*]\n<br />[*]Eugene[/*]\n<br />[*]Faust[/*]\n<br />[*]Fleurine[/*]\n<br />[*]Hakan[/*]\n<br />[*]Isla[/*]\n<br />[*]Ivaras[/*]\n<br />[*]Juna[/*]\n<br />[*]Katrielle[/*]\n<br />[*]Lacey[/*]\n<br />[*]Lucia[/*]\n<br />[*]Lucikiel[/*]\n<br />[*]Lumen[/*]\n<br />[*]Miriam[/*]\n<br />[*]Mirren[/*]\n<br />[*]Mister Ginger[/*]\n<br />[*]Nagito[/*]\n<br />[*]Nino[/*]\n<br />[*]Nora[/*]\n<br />[*]Quinn[/*]\n<br />[*]Ripley[/*]\n<br />[*]Rodney[/*]\n<br />[*]Roswell (The Wayfarer)[/*]\n<br />[*]Sen (Lurking in the Dark)[/*]\n<br />[*]Shiko[/*]\n<br />[*]Sirona[/*]\n<br />[*]Sorren[/*]\n<br />[*]Tea[/*]\n<br />[*]Teddy[/*]\n<br />[*]Theo[/*]\n<br />[*]Tilly[/*]\n<br />[*]Valko[/*]\n<br />[*]Wilford[/*]\n<br />[/list][/*]\n<br />[/list][/spoiler]\n<br />[left][color=#D4D4D8][b][size=5][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/54530]Cindersap Forest Compatibility[/url] Edition[/size][/b][/color][/left]\n<br />[list]\n<br />[*][color=#D4D4D8][size=4]built to go with Forest Compatibility Patch. It includes everything above, plus fixes for NPC spots the forest patch changes. Install this or the standalone version, not both.[/size][/color][/*]\n<br />[/list][b][size=5]Installation instructions[/size][/b]